lesson: 240
title: US coins
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: In the United States a penny is 1 cent, a nickel 5 cents, a dime 10 cents and a quarter 25 cents; 100 cents make a dollar.
explain: Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.
explain: 2 quarters, 3 dimes, 1 nickel and 4 pennies: 50 + 30 + 5 + 4 = 89 cents.
vars: a=name q=2..3 d=2..6 n=2..4 p=2..9
answer: q * 25 + d * 10 + n * 5 + p
exercise: {a} has {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents does {a.he} have?
exercise: In a piggy bank there are {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How much money is that in cents?
exercise: How many cents are {p} pennies, {n} nickels, {d} dimes and {q} quarters worth together?
exercise: {a} empties {a.his} pocket: {d} dimes, {q} quarters, {p} pennies and {n} nickels. How many cents does {a.he} have?
exercise: The change from a store is {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents is the change?
exercise: got {q} quarters {d} dimes {n} nickels n {p} pennies. how many cents
exercise: {q} quarters, {d+1} dimes — no wait {d} dimes, {n} nickels, {p} pennies. how much in cents
exercise: piggy bank: {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels, {p} pennies, oh and a button lol. cents?
exercise: my lil sis says {q+d+n+p} cents cos {q+d+n+p} coins. nah, {q} quarters {d} dimes {n} nickels {p} pennies. how many cents really
exercise: y'all, found {p} pennies n {n} nickels in the couch, plus {d} dimes n {q} quarters in my jacket. how many cents total
test: What is the value in cents of {d} dimes, {p} pennies, {q} quarters and {n} nickels?
test: A jar holds {n} nickels, {q} quarters, {p} pennies and {d} dimes. Find the amount in cents.
test: coins on the table: {q} quarters, {n} nickels, {d} dimes, {p} pennies. cents?
test: {a} pays with exactly {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents did the toy cost?
test: how much is {d} dimes + {q} quarters + {p} pennies + {n} nickels in cents
test: {a} has a dollar bill at home, but in {a.his} pocket there are {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents are in the pocket?
exam: Determine the aggregate value, expressed in cents, of {q.words} quarters, {d.words} dimes, {n.words} nickels and {p.words} pennies.
exam: It is given that a receptacle contains {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. Ascertain the total monetary value thereof in cents.
exam: Compute the sum, in cents, tendered by {a} in respect of {p} pennies, {n} nickels, {d} dimes and {q} quarters.
exam: Whereas the coins in question comprise {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies of United States currency, state their combined value in cents.
exercise: Great-aunt May passed away and left {a} her piggy bank with {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies in it. How many cents is that?
exercise: dad's between jobs so it's the swear jar or nothing. {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels, {p} pennies in the damn thing. how many cents?
test: {a} told a white lie and said {a.his} pocket was empty. In fact it held {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {n} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents was {a.he} hiding?
